		{
			dependencies: ["6197C51E04761371"]
			description: [
				"The &6Machine Controller&r is a cover that manages the operation of &bGregTech&r machines, similar to a &aSoft Mallet&r. These are crucial for &epassive automation&r, where a machine is dedicated to keeping something in stock for you."
				""
				"\"Machines\" here is broader than you might think. It of course works on single-block machines, but can also be used on &eMultiblock Controllers&r like your &3Electronic Blast Furnace&r. But it's even more flexible than that: you can use it on &eany &bGregTech&e block that accepts transfer covers&r, as long as the controllable cover is placed on it first! This means it also works for things like &6Chests&r, &6Drums&r, and Multiblock inputs."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The cover works by detecting a &eredstone signal&r. By default, the entire machine will be disabled if a sufficiently strong signal is detected by the cover."
				""
				"When you open the Machine Controller's GUI with a &aScrewdriver&r, you will see several options for configuring its behavior:"
				""
				"The strength of the signal required to trigger the Machine Controller is configurable using the top slider."
				""
				"Another button allows you to select whether to control the whole machine (where applicable) or a specific cover. This lets you do things like stop moving items into a machine, but also allow the machine to continue working."
				""
				"Switching from &eNormal&r to &eInverted&r mode will make the Machine Controller instead disable the machine until it receives the requisite redstone signal. This is often preferable when working with &6Level Emitters&r to prevent machines from starting up if your &eME Network&r is offline."
			]
			id: "1C06BD3B0CC3681D"
			rewards: [{
				id: "0F782759F1D60871"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "3ACF0778B18516E0"
				item: "gtceu:machine_controller_cover"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -3.0d
			y: -3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"3B639F4061B00F1A"
				"5C4E189A3E401566"
			]
			description: [
				"The &3Extruder&r is an alternative way to form shapes from metal. &aExtruder Shapes&r are used for telling an Extruder which shape to make."
				""
				"Extruders are &2not strictly needed for any recipe, but often provide single-step or tool-free alternaives to other methods.&r Extruders use ingots, but are as efficient for making &6Gears&r as melting and solidifying. They are also the most efficient way to make &6Bolts&r, &6Small Gears&r, and &6Rings&r."
				""
				"You can also use Extruders to make things from other machines like plates and wires, but they take more energy than using the dedicated machines for these purposes."
				""
				"&2There is also an LV version, but most of the Extruder's recipes must be run at MV or higher."
			]
			icon: "gtceu:mv_extruder"
			id: "39F50550E5B616CF"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6C46EE6E0C2B63DE"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
